Don't prioritise drain resistance. Sure, swap out your amulet for "oDR
when you are entering a particularly drainy level (ie the guild) but
otherwise it's not really an issue. A buffed character will kill 90%
of drain-threats before they get close enough to attack, and then 90%
of those attacks will fail to get through anyway. Lost levels can
usually be regained immediately anyway, just kill something quickly.

WW boots or permanent levitation/ flight/ magical breathing, on the
other hand, are an absolute necessity, to counter the splashy spell of
instadeath.



